<title>UK: IFC sets six tranche equity-linked peseta bond.</title>
<headline>IFC sets six tranche equity-linked peseta bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corporation has issued a six tranche equity linked bond for a total of 38 billion peseta, sole lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said. All tranches have a variable coupon linked to a basket of FTSE, DAX, CAC and IBEX indices. All bonds will mature in August 2002. There are varying redemption amounts for each tranche plus 157.90 percent of the basket.</p>
<p>The bonds are issued at par. Pay date is February 17, 1997. All the bonds will be listed on Madrid and the denominations are one million. Further terms were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7658</p>
